==English==

===Etymology===
Named for {{w|Max Planck}} (1858–1947), German theoretical physicist, who discovered it in 1900.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{head|en|noun|head=[[Planck]]'s [[constant]]}}

# {{context|physics|lang=en}} the [[constant]] of [[proportionality]] (symbol '''''h'''''), relating the [[energy]] and [[frequency]] of a [[photon]] (6.626 x 10<sup>-34</sup> [[joule]]-[[second]]s); also related to the [[indeterminacy]] [[limit]] in the [[Heisenberg uncertainty principle]]; the [[quantum]] of [[action]]

